N2  - INTERVENTION: Product Name: PSILOCYBINE, Product Code:PRD10762858, Pharmaceutical Form: CAPSULE FOR ORAL USE, Other descriptive name: , Strength: , Product Name: PSILOCYBINE, Product Code:PRD13720396, Pharmaceutical Form: CAPSULE FOR ORAL USE, Other descriptive name: , Strength:, CONDITION: Alcohol use disorder, depressive symptoms ; MedDRA version: 21.1Level: PTClassification code: 10054089Term: Depressive symptom Class: 100000004873 ; MedDRA version: 20.1Level: PTClassification code: 10080021Term: Alcohol use disorder Class: 100000004873 Therapeutic area: Psychiatry and Psychology [F] - Mental Disorders [F03], PRIMARY OUTCOME: Main Objective: Evaluate the efficacy of administering 2 high doses of 25mg psilocybin 3 weeks apart, compared with administering 2 low doses of 3mg psilocybin 3 weeks apart, on the incidence of relapse in terms of excessive alcohol consumption, in patients with severe AUD and comorbid depression following detoxification, over a period of 6 months. Primary end point(s): Time to relapse is defined as the 1st heavy drinking day (HDD), i.e., =60g alcohol. Alcohol consumption will be collected every 6 weeks using the Timeline Follow-Back (TLFB) method, with the assistance of either a digital or paper calendar. Secondary Objective: Compare 2 groups (High dose (HD) vs low dose (LD)) over the first 6 months in terms of changes in:  1) drinking outcomes,  2) craving,  3) alcohol-related quality of life,  4) depressive symptoms 5) psychological functioning., Describe, by group (HD and LD), the proportion and characteristics of participants requesting a 3rd dose of 25mg psilocybin at week 27 (patient-preference) 1) drinking outcomes,  2) craving,  3) alcohol-related quality of life,  4) depressive symptoms 5) psychological functioning. 6) preference for a 3rd dose 7) administration of 3rd dose requesting a 3rd dose of 25mg, In the subgroups of non-relapsers at 6 months from LD (NRLD) and HD (NRHD): describe maintenance of absence of relapse and changes between 6 & 12 months (from week 27 to week 51) in outcomes 1-5 (see A) in groups “administration 3rd dose” (A3D) vs “no 3rd dose” (N3D), In the subgroups of relapsers at 6 months from LD group (RLD) and HD (RHD): describe changes between 6 & 12 months (from week 27 to week 51) in outcomes 1-5 in A3D vs. N3D., In the high dose group: describe changes from baseline in outcomes 1-5 between 6-12 months in A3D vs. N3D and in the whole group., Response factors., Safety and tolerance over 24 months., Blood tests between baseline and week 28 and percentage in norms at week 28, INCLUSION CRITERIA: Confirmed DSM-5 diagnosis of severe AUD., Scale BDI-II ((Beck Depression Inventory) =14, The last drink must have been consumed between day(D) -60 and D -10 at the inclusion visit. The patient must have had at least 1 HDD during the last drinking period NB: The last drinking period before inclusion is defined by the last 4 weeks counted from the last drink., Patient who has provided informed and voluntary consent., Patient affiliated with or beneficiary of a health insurance plan., Adult patient (=18 years)., SECONDARY OUTCOME: Secondary end point(s):By group HD and LD will be assessed at weeks 0, 3, 9, 15, 21, 27 : TLFB, CEQ, AQoLS- brief, BDI-II, BAI, DERS, A-RSQ, PCL-5, VPT only week 0, 3 and 28. Secondary end point(s):By group HD and LD, the proportion and characteristics of participants requesting a 3rd dose of 25mg psilocybin will be assessed at weeks 27 : TLFB, CEQ, AQoLS- brief, BDI-II, BAI, DERS, A-RSQ, PCL-5, preference for a 3rd dose, Administration of a 3rd dose Secondary end point(s):In the groups HD or LD and subgroups relapsers or no-relapsers describe changes of blood samples between baseline and week 28 Secondary end point(s):In the high dose group: changes from baseline between 6-12 months in the subgroups A3D vs. N3D and in the whole group will be assessed : TLFB, CEQ, AQoLS-brief, BDI-II, BAI, DERS, A-RSQ, PCL-5. Secondary end point(s):In the subgroups 