N2  - The goal of this clinical trial is to determine the safety and efficacy of psilocybinassisted Therapy (PAT) in individuals with comorbid Major Depressive Disorder (MDD) andAlcohol Use Disorder (AUD). The main question it aims to answer is:- What is the feasibility and safety of administering PAT in adults with MDD-AUD byevaluating recruitment, retention, tolerability, and safety?Researchers will compare the psilocybin (25 mg) and placebo groups to see if there areany significant differences in frequency of dropouts or serious adverse events.Participants will:  -  be randomized to receive either psilocybin (25 mg) or placebo  -  visit the site (in-person and remotely) for a total of 14 times to complete studytasks  -  receive psilocybin-assisted therapy (PAT) at five various timepoints
