T1  - Mindfulness and Psilocybin in Healthy Adults: a Comparative Study
T2  - The Mindful Psilocybin Study: a three-arm, open-label, randomised controlled pilot trial in healthy volunteers examining the interaction between mindfulness training and psilocybin on wellbeing and psychological, physiological and behavioural measures


Y1  - 2026//
Y2  - 2026//
N2  - INTERVENTION: This study includes three intervention conditions:  1. Psilocybin alone 2. Mindfulness alone (described under Comparator/Control Treatment) 3. Combined mindfulness plus psilocybin  Psilocybin intervention Participants will receive a single oral dose of psilocybin (25 mg tablet) administered on-site under medical and psychological supervision.  The intervention includes: -Preparation: two sessions (one online, 2 weeks prior; one in-person, 1 week prior) -Dosing session: supervised administration with two trained facilitators; safety screening conducted on the day (pregnancy, alcohol, and drug use); participants must nominate a support person for transport -Integration: two sessions (one in-person the day after dosing; one online within the following week)  All procedures follow established best-practice approaches for participant preparation, safety monitoring, and psychological support used in prior clinical psilocybin trials.  Adherence/accountability: on-site administration under staff supervision with full drug accountability.  Combined intervention Participants complete the 4-week online mindfulness program (see Comparator/Control) followed by psilocybin dosing in Week 5, with identical preparation, dosing, and integration procedures as above., CONDITION: Mental Health - Studies of normal psychology, cognitive function and behaviour Mental Wellbeing; ; Mental Wellbeing, PRIMARY OUTCOME: Wellbeing[Warwick Edinburgh Mental Wellbeing Scale Baseline (5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group), primary endpoint (3 weeks post-dose/3 weeks after the end of the structured mindfulness training), long-term follow-up (3, 6 and 12 months post-primary endpoint)], SECONDARY OUTCOME: Aberrant meaning making[Bullshit Receptivity Scale Baseline (T1) ; T2 (during dosing for psilocybin groups; end of structured phase for mindfulness-only group) - approximately 4 hours post-dosing ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment)] Absorption[Modified Tellegen Absorption Scale (MODTAS) Baseline (T1) ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Acceptance and avoidance during acute effects of psilocybin[Acceptance/Avoidance Promoting Experiences Questionnaire (APEQ) (psilocybin-only and combined psilocybin/mindfulness groups only) 1-day post-dosing] Acceptance[Acceptance and Action Questionnaire-II (AAQ-II) The Acceptance and Action Questionnaire-II will be assessed at: ; Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Alcohol Consumption[Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test (AUDIT) Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Altered states of consciousness (psilocybin-only and combined psilocybin/mindfulness groups only)[11D-Altered States of Consciousness 1-day post-dose] Avoidance[Brief Experiential Avoidance Questionnaire (BEAQ) Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Challenging experiences during the acute effects of psilocybin[Challenging Experiences Questionnaire (CEQ) (psilocybin-only and combined psilocybin/mindfulness groups only) 1-day post-dose] Convergent/divergent thinking[Remote Associations Task Baseline (T1) ; T2 (during dosing for psilocybin groups; end of structured phase for mindfulness-only group) - approximately 4 hours post-dosing ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment)] Depression, anxiety, stress[Depression Anxiety Stress Scale - 21 Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Diet[Rapid Eating Assessment for Patients Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Explore-exploit dynamics[Patch Foraging Task Baseline (T1) ; T2 (during dosing for psilocybin groups; end of structured phase for mindfulness-only group) - approximately 4 hours post-dosing ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment)] Heart rate Variability[Heart rate variability - assessed through EEG Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; ] Hysteresis effect[Visual Hysteresis Task Baseline (T1) ; T2 (during dosing for psilocybin groups; end of structured phase for mindfulness-only group) - approximately 4 hours post-dosing ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment)] Insight misattribution[Anagram insight misattribution task Baseline (T1) ; T2 (during dosing for psilocybin groups; end of structured phase for mindfulness-only group) - approximately 4 hours post-dosing ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment)] Insight[Insight Dimensions Matri X(all groups) T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T5 (3 months after T4 outcome measures)] Interoceptive Awareness[Multidimentional Assessment of Interoceptive Awareness - 2 Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Intolerance of Uncertainty[Intolerance of Uncertainty Scale Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Life satisfaction [Satisfaction with Life Questionnaire Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Meditative depth[Meditation Depth Inde X(MEDI) Primary endpoint (3 weeks post-dose/post-mindfulness training), long-term follow-up (3, 6 and 12 months post-primary endpoint)] Mindfulness[Five Facet Mindfulness Questionnaire (FFMQ) Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Mystical experiences (psilocybin-only and combined psilocybin/mindfulness groups only)[Revised Mystical Experiences Questionnaire (MEQ-30) 1-day post-dose] Nicotine consumption[Nicotine consumption questionnaire (study specific questionnaire) Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Pain sensitivity[Cold Water Pressor Test Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment)] Pain tolerance[Cold Water Pressor Test ;  Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T3 (one day post-dose/post T2) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; ] Pattern recognition[Snowy Pictures Task (SPT) Baseline (T1) ; T2 (during dosing for psilocybin groups; end of structured phase for mindfulness-only group) - approximately 4 hours post-dosing ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment)] Perceived barriers to meditation[Determinants of Meditation Practice Inventory - Revised (DMPI-R) Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; ] Physical Activity[International Physical Activity Questionnaire Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Safety measure: Adverse Events[Adverse events (self and clinician reported). Adverse events may include physiological effects (headache, increased blood pressure, nausea) and psychological effects (distress, anxiety). Blood pressure measurements will occur during dosing. Adverse events during dosing will be assessed by patient self-report and clinical examination. Adverse events after dosing will be assessed using study-specific questionnaires. Baseline (T1) ; T2 (during dosing for psilocybin groups; end of structured phase for mindfulness-only group) ; T3 (one day post-T2 / post-dosing) ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Safety measure: Hallucinogen persisting perception disorder[Hallucinogen persisting perception disorder questionnaire T5 (3 months after T4 outcome measures)] Self-compassion[Self-Compassion Scale Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Sensitivity to bodily signals of anxiety[Anxiety Sensitivity Inde XBaseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Somatic symptom burden[Somatic Symptoms Scale Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)] Time spent practicing[Time spent practicing - participants will record their meditation practice in a diary/meditation log Baseline (T1) - 5 weeks pre-dose in psilocybin-only group, one day before start of mindfulness intervention in mindfulness-only and combined group ; T4 (3 weeks post-dosing/post-T2; 9 weeks post-enrolment) ; T5, T6, T7 (3, 6, 12 months after T4 outcome measures)], INCLUSION CRITERIA: -Be aged 18 to 75 years.  -Be medically stable, as determined by screening for medical problems via a personal interview, a medical questionnaire, a physical examination, an electrocardiogram (ECG), and routine medical blood laboratory tests.  -If of childbearing potential, must not be pregnant or breast-feeding at screening, must have a negative pregnancy test prior to dosing session, and must agree to use adequate birth control from screening through 10 days after the dosing session.
