N2  - The German psilocybin compassionate use programme represents a regulatory milestone and a pragmatic step toward integrating psychedelicassisted therapy into mainstream psychiatric care. Alongside developments in Australia and elsewhere, the introduction of the programme invites the psychiatric community to consider how expanded access programmes can be leveraged not only to address urgent clinical needs but also to strengthen the scientific foundations for these emerging treatments. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2026 APA, all rights reserved)
