Y1  - 2023//
N2  - Psilocybin is an alkaloid found in multiple species of fungi within the genus Psilocybe. Refractory existential distress, anxiety, and depression affect many patients facing a short prognosis due to a serious illness. Unfortunately, traditional psychotherapy-oriented approaches have shown limited efficacy for these symptoms and/or may not always be feasible in this patient population. Early data suggest psilocybin is a promising modality for end-of-life anxiety, depression, and existential distress when utilized under the guidance of a guide or therapist. However, its use is limited currently outside of a clinical trial. Clinicians who care for patients with serious illness should inquire about its nonprescribed use. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
