Y1  - 2024//
N2  - Comments on an article by Sipan Haikazian et al.(see record 2024-23559-001). Psilocybin, a 5-HT 2 A receptor agonist, has shown potential efficacy in treating depression. The authors conducted a thorough meta-analysis, comprehensively assessing the effect of psilocybin on depressive symptoms in patients diagnosed with life-threatening illnesses or major depressive disorder. We acknowledge the contributions made by the authors. However, we identified some flaws in the publication at hand. In section 3.3 "Efficacy of PAP", the authors mentioned that "a pooled standard mean difference (SMD) between experimental and control arms in depression outcomes across all included studies was-0.78, indicating a large and significant effect".We agree with the authors' statement that psilocybin has a significantly greater antidepressant effect compared to the comparator arms. Well-designed phase III trials are urgently needed to optimize psilocybin dosage and minimize the potential for functional unblinding by incorporating active comparators. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
