N2  - Comments on an article by S. Marwaha et al. (see record 2023-39660-025). Steven Marwaha et al. wrote an intriguing Review about new treatments for major depression. My concern is with regard to figure 2 of the Review, which shows the location of the effects of new treatments for depression. The figure shows that psilocybin affected seven locations (two locations of the default mode network [DMN], three of the salience network [SN], and two of the executive network [EN]), whereas ketamine affected four locations. Another concern is a lack of descrip tion of new psychotherapy for depression, although the authors focused on biological treatments. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
